-- Employment Relations Act 2000 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act's text, the Legislation
-- Act 2019 working day and s 55, and the calendar (the King's Birthday 1 June
-- 2026 and 4 June 2029; 1 January 2027 a Friday).

§ `Tests`

mat MEANS LIST Date 10 7 2026, Date 25 6 2027, Date 14 7 2028, Date 6 7 2029

GIVEN trial IS A MAYBE NUMBER, before IS A BOOLEAN, notice IS A DATE, pay IS A NUMBER, held IS A NUMBER, optout IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Employment
job trial before notice pay held optout MEANS Employment OF Date 2 3 2026, before, trial, notice, pay, held, 200000, optout

GIVEN g IS A Ground, related IS A BOOLEAN, occurred IS A DATE, noticed IS A DATE, raised IS A DATE, consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Grievance
grievance g related occurred noticed raised consent MEANS Grievance OF g, related, occurred, noticed, raised, consent, FALSE, mat

dismissal MEANS grievance `(a) unjustifiable dismissal` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) FALSE

§§ `Trial provisions (ss 67A-67B)`

#ASSERT `the last day of the trial period for` (job (JUST 90) FALSE (Date 30 5 2026) 0 1 FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 5 2026)
#ASSERT `the grievance is barred` (job (JUST 90) FALSE (Date 30 5 2026) 0 1 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job (JUST 90) FALSE (Date 31 5 2026) 0 1 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job (JUST 90) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) 0 1 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job (JUST 91) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) 0 1 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job NOTHING FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) 0 1 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job (JUST 90) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) 0 1 FALSE) (grievance `(c) discrimination` FALSE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the grievance is barred` (job (JUST 90) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) 0 1 FALSE) (grievance `(b) unjustifiable disadvantage` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job (JUST 90) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) 0 1 FALSE) (grievance `(b) unjustifiable disadvantage` FALSE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) FALSE)

§§ `High earners (ss 67I-67J, 113A-113B)`

#ASSERT `the annual remuneration of` (job NOTHING FALSE (Date 1 9 2026) 100000 182 FALSE) EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `the grievance is barred` (job NOTHING FALSE (Date 1 9 2026) 200000 364 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job NOTHING FALSE (Date 1 9 2026) 199999 364 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT `the grievance is barred` (job NOTHING FALSE (Date 1 9 2026) 100000 182 FALSE) dismissal
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance is barred` (job NOTHING FALSE (Date 1 9 2026) 250000 364 TRUE) dismissal
#ASSERT `the remuneration threshold from` 200000 `, earnings this year` 1900 `, in the year of last increase` 1800 EQUALS 211111
#ASSERT `the remuneration threshold from` 200000 `, earnings this year` 1800 `, in the year of last increase` 1800 EQUALS 200000
-- A half rounds up (added after the independent pass).
#ASSERT `the remuneration threshold from` 200000 `, earnings this year` 400001 `, in the year of last increase` 400000 EQUALS 200001

§§ `Raising a grievance and time limits (ss 114, 120, 142)`

-- 90 days from 2 March 2026 end on Saturday 30 May; Monday 1 June is the
-- King's Birthday, so Tuesday 2 June (s 55).
#ASSERT `the last day to raise the grievance` dismissal EQUALS Date 2 6 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to raise the grievance` (grievance `(d) sexual harassment` FALSE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 3 2027
-- Legislation Act s 56 (added after the independent pass): 12 months from 29
-- February 2028 end at the close of 28 February 2029 (a Wednesday).
#ASSERT `the last day to raise the grievance` (grievance `(d) sexual harassment` FALSE (Date 29 2 2028) (Date 29 2 2028) (Date 15 5 2028) FALSE) EQUALS Date 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the last day to raise the grievance` (grievance `(a) unjustifiable dismissal` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) FALSE) EQUALS Date 8 7 2026
#ASSERT `the grievance was raised in time` (grievance `(a) unjustifiable dismissal` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the grievance was raised in time` (grievance `(a) unjustifiable dismissal` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 3 6 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the grievance was raised in time` (grievance `(a) unjustifiable dismissal` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 3 6 2026) TRUE)
-- 3 years from 2 June 2026 end on Saturday 2 June 2029; Monday 4 June is the
-- King's Birthday, so Tuesday 5 June.
#ASSERT `the last day to commence an action on a grievance raised on` (Date 2 6 2026) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 5 6 2029
#ASSERT `the last day to commence another action, cause arising on` (Date 16 10 2026) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 18 10 2032
#ASSERT `the last day to request reasons for a dismissal on` (Date 1 10 2026) `, learned of on` (Date 5 10 2026) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 4 12 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to give the statement of reasons, request received` (Date 16 10 2026) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 30 10 2026
-- 14 days from 11 December end on 25 December: the next working day is 5
-- January 2027 (1 January a Friday, so 4 January is not one).
#ASSERT `the last day to give the statement of reasons, request received` (Date 11 12 2026) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 5 1 2027

§§ `Remedies (ss 123B-128)`

GIVEN contributed IS A BOOLEAN, serious IS A BOOLEAN, reduction IS A NUMBER, lost IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Remedy facts`
remedy contributed serious reduction lost MEANS `Remedy facts` OF contributed, serious, reduction, lost, 15000

#ASSERT `the reimbursement the Authority must order` (remedy FALSE FALSE 0 20000) EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `the reimbursement the Authority must order` (remedy FALSE FALSE 0 10000) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the reimbursement the Authority must order` (remedy TRUE FALSE 20 20000) EQUALS 12000
#ASSERT `the reimbursement the Authority must order` (remedy TRUE TRUE 20 20000) EQUALS 0
-- Changed after the independent pass: a reduction over 100% is refused
-- (s 124(2)), so the earlier assertion that 150% gives 0 is removed; 100%
-- gives 0.
#ASSERT `the reimbursement the Authority must order` (remedy TRUE FALSE 100 20000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reinstatement and compensation are available` (remedy FALSE FALSE 0 20000)
#ASSERT NOT `reinstatement and compensation are available` (remedy TRUE FALSE 20 20000)

§§ `The top-level goal`

#ASSERT `the grievance position for` (job NOTHING FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) 100000 364 FALSE) `, grievance` dismissal `, remedies` (remedy FALSE FALSE 0 20000) EQUALS `Grievance position` OF FALSE, TRUE, Date 2 6 2026, Date 15 5 2029, TRUE, 15000
#ASSERT `the grievance position for` (job (JUST 90) FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) 100000 364 FALSE) `, grievance` dismissal `, remedies` (remedy FALSE FALSE 0 20000) EQUALS `Grievance position` OF TRUE, TRUE, Date 2 6 2026, Date 15 5 2029, FALSE, 0

§§ `Regression: a Sunday 1 January`

-- 1 January 2023 was a Sunday: Monday 2 and Tuesday 3 January are not working
-- days, and Wednesday 4 January is (Legislation Act 2019 s 13(d); corrected
-- after the Electricity Industry Act independent pass found it).
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 2 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 3 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 4 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat
